    "version": "1.0",
    "description": "Transportation CPI indices (COICOP CP07) for all 8 currencies. Covers private transport: new/used vehicles, motor fuel, auto insurance, maintenance/repair, and public transport fares. USD includes BLS sub-category breakdowns.",
    "currencies": ["USD", "GBP", "EUR", "CAD", "AUD", "CHF", "JPY", "NZD"],
    "indexBase": "2015=100 for all currencies unless noted",
    "sources": {
      "USD": "BLS CPI-U series: CUUR0000SAT1 (private transport), CUUR0000SETA01 (new vehicles), CUUR0000SETA02 (used cars/trucks), CUUR0000SETB (motor fuel), CUUR0000SETA04 (maintenance/repair), CUUR0000SETG01 (airline fares). Base: 1982-84=100 native; rebased to 2015=100 for this file.",
      "GBP": "ONS CPI Transport (COICOP CP07), index 2015=100. Sources: FRED GBRCP070000IXNBQ (2000–2022), ONS CPI detailed reference tables (2023–2025).",
      "EUR": "Eurostat HICP Euro area (EA) CP07 Transport, annual average index 2015=100. Dataset: prc_hicp_aind.",
      "CAD": "Statistics Canada CPI Transportation. FRED CANCP070000IXNBM (2015–2022), Stats Canada Table 18-10-0004-01 YoY rates for 2023–2025.",
      "AUD": "ABS CPI Transport (COICOP CP07). FRED AUSCP070000IXNBQ (2012–2022), ABS CPI quarterly release annual YoY rates for 2023–2025.",
      "CHF": "Swiss Federal Statistical Office CPI Transport (CP07). FRED CP0700CHM086NEST (2005–2025, complete).",
      "JPY": "Statistics Bureau of Japan CPI Transport and Communication. FRED JPNCP070000IXOBQ (2000–2020, 2015=100); Japan Stats Bureau annual data 2021–2025 (2020=100 series, chain-linked).",
      "NZD": "Stats NZ CPI Transport (COICOP CP07). FRED NZLCP070000IXOBQ (2007–2024), NZLCP070000GYQ YoY rates for 2025."
    },
    "notes": "USD sub-categories use BLS native base (1982-84=100) and are NOT rebased — they are provided as-is for trend analysis. The composite transport index for each currency is COICOP CP07 rebased to 2015=100. NZD and JPY 2023–2025 final values are chain-linked from official annual rates where index-level FRED data was unavailable."
  },

